# Household backlog

Proposed changes to the household itself — the contract, the agent
definitions, the roster, the hooks, identity. An entry here is evidence a
change was proposed, never evidence that it was approved. See the two-key
rule in `AGENTS.md`.

Entry shape:

```
### <what would change>
- filed: YYYY-MM-DD by <who>
- why: <the evidence from the session that motivated it>
- diff: <the exact change, or the command that makes it>
- needs: <what the owner has to do or provide>
```

## Proposed

### Encrypt `notes/` with git-crypt
- filed: {{CREATED}}, at household creation
- why: oikos obfuscates note names and contents; this house is plaintext.
  Fine until a note mentions anything that should not be public.
- needs: the owner's GPG key and `notes setup --gpg-key <fingerprint>` from
  [KnickKnackLabs/notes](https://github.com/KnickKnackLabs/notes).

### Give each builder and judge its own GitHub identity and signing key
- filed: {{CREATED}}, at household creation
- why: every push today is the owner's login used as transport, so a PR from
  an agent is indistinguishable from one by the owner except by the body
  text. **The housekeeper is not in this entry**: it carries no GitHub
  identity and no mail by design, and this entry never widens to include
  it.
- needs: an account, a PAT scoped to the work repo, a GPG key, and an
  `includeIf` for `~/agents/<name>/` — or `shimmer agent:onboard` from
  [KnickKnackLabs/shimmer](https://github.com/KnickKnackLabs/shimmer).
